# Recorded baselines are machine-specific: absolute timings from one laptop are
# false regressions on every other machine, and a committed baseline.json would
# hand everyone else a permanently red comparison.
#
# A baseline that is genuinely worth sharing — one recorded on a dedicated,
# quiet machine — can be committed deliberately with `git add -f` and pointed at
# with `--baseline <path>`. The comparator skips absolute timings across
# machines by itself and still judges the portable metrics.
baselines/
